{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. You're here because you had a procedure today for your airway, and we want to keep an eye on you afterward. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:52:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, doctor. I’m feeling okay. A bit tired, but no pain. My breathing feels a little easier than before the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. The ENT and interventional pulmonology teams found significant narrowing in your left mainstem bronchus and bronchus intermedius again, so they did a dilation to open those areas up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:55:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so it came back? I thought the last dilation helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:56:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because of your underlying condition—polychondritis—the scarring and narrowing tend to recur. That’s why we’re also adjusting your medications to help reduce inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:58:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, the connective tissue disorder. So what’s changed with my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2134-10-18 20:59:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve increased your prednisone from 30 mg to 60 mg for two days to help calm the inflammation after the procedure. Then you’ll taper down—50 mg for two days, then 40 mg for two days, and back to your usual 30 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2134-10-18 21:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. But why the change now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2134-10-18 21:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because the procedure itself causes some inflammation, and with your history of stopping prednisone before, we want to make sure we prevent another flare-up like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2134-10-18 21:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I didn’t realize stopping it could cause such a problem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2134-10-18 21:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can, especially with your condition. Also, because you’re on long-term steroids, we’re starting you on Bactrim—one tablet daily—for infection prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2134-10-18 21:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve never taken that before. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2134-10-18 21:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most people tolerate it well. Just let us know if you develop a rash, fever, or any mouth sores. It’s mainly to protect you while your immune system is a bit suppressed from the steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2134-10-19 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your chest X-ray this morning looks stable—your trach is in place, lungs are clear. No signs of complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2134-10-19 09:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. My breathing still feels okay. I’m using the humidifier like always."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2134-10-19 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The humidified air helps keep your airway moist, especially with the trach. One lab note—your white blood cell count is elevated, about 19.2, but that’s likely from the steroids or the procedure, not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2134-10-19 09:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2134-10-19 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not in this case. You’re not running a fever, and your lungs sound stable. Steroids often raise the white count. We’ll monitor it, but no need for concern now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re getting ready to discharge you. You’re doing well—no shortness of breath, vitals stable. Just a few last things to go over."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the steroid taper as we discussed: 50 mg tomorrow, 40 mg the next two days, then back to 30 mg daily. Keep taking Bactrim daily, and stay on your famotidine and lactulose as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the humidifier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep using humidified air with your trach. It helps prevent dryness and thick secretions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:36:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, rheumatology will help set you up on Enbrel after discharge. Call their nurse to arrange delivery. You have follow-up appointments with rheumatology, ENT, and pulmonology—someone will call you with the pulmonology appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:37:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to call. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You tolerated the procedure well, and your recovery is on track. Just monitor your breathing—if you feel more short of breath, let someone know right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:40:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I feel much better than I did last time I was here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2134-10-19 15:41:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be heading home soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2134-10-18 20:51:00",
    "admission_end": "2134-10-19 17:03:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for management following a procedure to address recurrent airway stenosis. He underwent microlaryngoscopy with balloon dilation and bronchial dilation due to severe stenosis in the left mainstem bronchus and bronchus intermedius, complications of his underlying connective tissue disorder with polychondritis. Post-procedure, he was stabilized on supplemental humidified oxygen and started on a short-term prednisone taper (60 mg for two days, then step-down) and Bactrim for infection prophylaxis. His white blood cell count rose to 19.2, attributed to steroid use or procedural inflammation, with no signs of infection. He remained in no acute distress, with stable vital signs and a clear chest X-ray. He was discharged home with follow-up arranged in rheumatology, ENT, and pulmonology, and instructions to continue trach care with humidification and medication tapering.",
    "problems": [
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Unspecified diffuse connective tissue disease",
      "Other disorders of bone and cartilage",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Other diseases of trachea and bronchus",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Tracheostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
